<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρύζω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
			<u>Mul.</u>
			2.131
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Arat.
			948
		</span></i>, etc.: 
			Ep.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρύζεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.140
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτρυξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sopat.
					5
				</span></i>
			 codd.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγρυξεν</span> Schw., Kaibel),
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				112.8
			</span></i>: mostly used in pres. and impf.
				:—<i>make a low murmuring sound,</i> of the note of
			the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλολυγών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.291
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυγών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.89
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				229.24
			</span></i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stud.Ital.</u>
				1.80
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυγόζω</span>): metaph., of
			men, <i>mutter, murmur,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.311
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of liquids,
				<i>squirt out with a noise,</i> of diarrhoea, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				11
			</span></i>; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τὸ οὖρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.131
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Steril.</u>
				247
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>, seems to mean <i>comes by drops.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>creak,</i> of shoes, only in <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				37
			</span></i> (dub.). (Onomatop.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
